    {
      "name": "Open review writing",
      "kind": "card",
      "description": "A ruled editorial excerpt with stable serif prose and quiet reading links.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-af-review\"><h2>Hades</h2><p>Updated after more runs: Hades remains a sharp, generous roguelike.</p><a href=\"https://sidequest.appcalipse.com\">Read on Sidequest <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M7 17 17 7M7 7h10v10\"/></svg></a><a class=\"ds-af-source\" href=\"https://sidequest.appcalipse.com\">View source <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M7 17 17 7M7 7h10v10\"/></svg></a></article>",
      "css": ".ds-af-review{padding:28px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line,#d0d3d5);color:var(--ink,#111b28)}.ds-af-review h2{font:400 clamp(26px,2.7vw,40px)/1.13 \"DM Serif Display\",Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0 0 13px}.ds-af-review p{font:19px/1.6 Georgia,\"Times New Roman\",serif;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;max-width:65ch;margin:20px 0}.ds-af-review a{display:inline-flex;gap:7px;align-items:center;position:relative;min-height:36px;padding:7px 0;margin-right:22px;font:11px 'DM Sans',sans-serif;text-decoration:none;color:var(--accent,#b33326)}.ds-af-review a.ds-af-source{color:var(--muted,#576172)}.ds-af-review a svg{width:15px}.ds-af-review a:after{content:\"\";height:1px;background:var(--accent,#b33326);position:absolute;bottom:3px;left:0;right:0;transform:scaleX(.16);transform-origin:left;transition:transform 180ms cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1)}.ds-af-review a:hover:after,.ds-af-review a:focus-visible:after{transform:scaleX(1)}.ds-af-review a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent,#b33326);outline-offset:3px;}@media(max-width:560px){.ds-af-review p{font-size:19px;line-height:1.65}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-af-review a:after{transition:none}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Critic's Column",
    "overview": "Afterword gives the reviewer a light editorial home. Deep ink, an expressive serif and vermilion details establish an identity independent from Sidequest. Thin rules and open columns create structure without enclosing every piece of writing in a card. This is the implemented world selected through Afterword A.\n\nThe author's perspective leads; real game covers act as reading anchors. Serif review prose carries the voice, while a quiet sans-serif handles dates, platforms, feedback and links. Public account details remain available without competing with the name, bio and writing.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Near-white paper, deep ink and restrained vermilion.",
      "Expressive serif headings, readable serif prose and sans-serif metadata.",
      "Open editorial columns separated by thin rules.",
      "Real portrait cover inserts and circular initials."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Accent Rule",
        "body": "Use vermilion for identity, ratings and useful link emphasis; let ink and paper carry the reading surface.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Author's Voice Rule",
        "body": "Let expressive serif headings and stable serif prose lead; keep interaction labels and record metadata in the quieter sans-serif voice.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Open Page Rule",
        "body": "Keep reviews and directory entries open on the canvas; use rules and spacing for separation before introducing enclosing panels.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve real reviewer names, bios, prose, platform labels and reputation values.",
      "**Do** use self-hosted DM Serif Display for identity and Georgia for the implemented reading body.",
      "**Do** keep cover images proportional, square-cornered and sourced from the real catalog.",
      "**Do** preserve generous mobile reading text, keyboard focus and reduced-motion behavior.",
      "**Do** keep source links and optional account details available in a secondary role."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** import Sidequest's dark surfaces, citron actions or condensed display type.",
      "**Don't** turn open review rows into a stack of elevated cards.",
      "**Don't** animate the reading column or make the prose move during ordinary reading.",
      "**Don't** copy invented comp prose, counts or a generated portrait into the product.",
      "**Don't** make technical account terminology the main promise of the reviewer page."
    ]
  }
}
